
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Mind Matters | Mental Health Guide</title>

<style>
* {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  scroll-behavior: smooth;
}

:root {
  --navy: #293b50;
  --blue: #66869b;
  --yellow: #f4d77e;
  --cream: #fffaf0;
  --lavender: #e9e4f2;
  --lightblue: #e8f0f5;
  --text: #455468;
  --white: #ffffff;
}

body {
  font-family: 'Trebuchet MS', Arial, sans-serif;
  background: #fcfbf8;
  color: var(--text);
  line-height: 1.7;
}

/* NAVIGATION */

header {
  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.96);
  border-bottom: 1px solid #e9e8e4;
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
  z-index: 100;
}

nav {
  max-width: 1150px;
  margin: auto;
  padding: 17px 30px;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 15px;
}

.logo {
  font-size: 23px;
  font-weight: bold;
  color: var(--navy);
  letter-spacing: 1px;
}

.logo span {
  color: #b9943f;
}

nav a {
  color: var(--text);
  text-decoration: none;
  margin-left: 18px;
  font-size: 14px;
  transition: .3s;
}

nav a:hover {
  color: #b9943f;
}

/* HERO */

.hero {
  min-height: 520px;
  background: linear-gradient(115deg, #e8f0f5 0%, #f0eaf5 55%, #fff3ce 100%);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  padding: 70px 9%;
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.hero::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  width: 350px;
  height: 350px;
  border: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,.65);
  border-radius: 50%;
  right: -90px;
  top: -100px;
}

.hero-content {
  max-width: 760px;
  position: relative;
  z-index: 1;
}

.tag {
  color: #71869a;
  font-size: 12px;
  letter-spacing: 3px;
  font-weight: bold;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}

.hero h1 {
  color: var(--navy);
  font-size: clamp(42px, 6vw, 68px);
  line-height: 1.12;
  margin: 20px 0;
}

.hero h1 span {
  color: #b9943f;
}

.hero p {
  max-width: 600px;
  font-size: 17px;
  margin-bottom: 25px;
}

.button {
  display: inline-block;
  background: var(--navy);
  color: white;
  padding: 13px 26px;
  text-decoration: none;
  border-radius: 7px;
  font-size: 14px;
  transition: .3s;
}

.button:hover {
  background: #526e83;
  transform: translateY(-2px);
}

/* GENERAL SECTIONS */

section {
  padding: 85px 9%;
  scroll-margin-top: 75px;
}

.section-label {
  text-align: center;
  color: #b9943f;
  font-size: 12px;
  letter-spacing: 3px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  font-weight: bold;
}

section h2 {
  color: var(--navy);
  text-align: center;
  font-size: 34px;
  margin: 8px 0 15px;
}

.description {
  text-align: center;
  max-width: 720px;
  margin: 0 auto 40px;
  color: #697789;
}

/* CARDS */

.cards {
  max-width: 1100px;
  margin: auto;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr));
  gap: 22px;
}

.card {
  background: white;
  padding: 30px;
  border-radius: 13px;
  border: 1px solid #e8e8e5;
  box-shadow: 0 7px 22px rgba(40,55,75,.045);
  transition: .3s;
}

.card:hover {
  transform: translateY(-5px);
  box-shadow: 0 12px 28px rgba(40,55,75,.09);
}

.card-number {
  font-size: 13px;
  letter-spacing: 2px;
  color: #b9943f;
  font-weight: bold;
  margin-bottom: 14px;
}

.card h3 {
  color: var(--navy);
  font-size: 19px;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
}

.card p {
  color: #697789;
  font-size: 14px;
}

.card.blue {
  border-top: 4px solid #9dbdce;
}

.card.yellow {
  border-top: 4px solid #e8cf85;
}

.card.purple {
  border-top: 4px solid #bdb0d6;
}

.card.green {
  border-top: 4px solid #a9c8b0;
}

/* HIGHLIGHT */

.highlight {
  background: var(--lightblue);
}

.quote {
  max-width: 850px;
  margin: auto;
  padding: 48px 35px;
  text-align: center;
  background: white;
  border-radius: 14px;
  border-left: 5px solid var(--yellow);
}

.quote p {
  font-size: 23px;
  color: var(--navy);
  font-weight: bold;
}

.quote span {
  display: block;
  margin-top: 12px;
  color: #8a929c;
  font-size: 13px;
}

/* SUPPORT */

.support-box {
  max-width: 850px;
  margin: auto;
  background: var(--cream);
  border: 1px solid #f0e7cf;
  border-radius: 14px;
  padding: 35px;
}

.support-box h3 {
  color: var(--navy);
  margin-bottom: 12px;
}

/* FOOTER */

footer {
  background: var(--navy);
  color: white;
  padding: 45px 9%;
  text-align: center;
}

footer h2 {
  font-size: 25px;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}

footer p {
  color: #d4dce4;
  font-size: 13px;
  margin: 5px;
}

.footer-line {
  width: 55px;
  height: 3px;
  background: var(--yellow);
  margin: 20px auto;
}

/* MOBILE */

@media(max-width: 700px) {
  nav {
    justify-content: center;
  }

  nav a {
    margin: 5px 8px;
  }

  .hero {
    padding: 65px 8%;
  }

  section {
    padding: 65px 7%;
  }

  section h2 {
    font-size: 28px;
  }

  .quote p {
    font-size: 19px;
  }
}
</style>
</head>

<body>

<header>
<nav>
  <div class="logo">MIND<span>MATTERS.</span></div>

  <div>
    <a href="#about">About</a>
    <a href="#stress">Stress</a>
    <a href="#selfesteem">Self-esteem</a>
    <a href="#habits">Healthy Habits</a>
    <a href="#support">Support</a>
  </div>
</nav>
</header>

<!-- HOME -->

<div class="hero">
  <div class="hero-content">
    <div class="tag">A STUDENT'S GUIDE TO MENTAL HEALTH</div>

    <h1>Your mind deserves <span>care</span>, too.</h1>

    <p>
      Being a teenager comes with different challenges.
      Academic pressure, social expectations and personal
      changes can sometimes feel overwhelming. This guide
      is here to help you understand your emotions and
      discover simple ways to take care of yourself.
    </p>

    <a href="#about" class="button">DISCOVER THE GUIDE</a>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ABOUT -->

<section id="about">
  <div class="section-label">01 — UNDERSTANDING YOURSELF</div>
  <h2>What Is Mental Health?</h2>

  <p class="description">
    Mental health is an important part of our overall well-being.
    It influences how we think, feel, face challenges, make decisions
    and interact with other people.
  </p>

  <div class="cards">

    <div class="card blue">
      <div class="card-number">01 / AWARENESS</div>
      <h3>Understand Your Emotions</h3>
      <p>
        Learning to recognize your emotions can help you
        understand what you need. Every emotion is valid,
        even the difficult ones.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card purple">
      <div class="card-number">02 / EXPRESSION</div>
      <h3>Express Yourself</h3>
      <p>
        Talking about your thoughts and feelings with someone
        you trust can help you feel heard and supported.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card yellow">
      <div class="card-number">03 / ACCEPTANCE</div>
      <h3>Accept Your Feelings</h3>
      <p>
        You do not have to pretend to be happy all the time.
        Difficult days are part of life, and your feelings matter.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- STRESS -->

<section id="stress" class="highlight">
  <div class="section-label">02 — EVERYDAY CHALLENGES</div>
  <h2>Managing Stress</h2>

  <p class="description">
    School responsibilities, exams and personal expectations
    can create stress. These small strategies may help you
    manage challenging situations.
  </p>

  <div class="cards">

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-number">TIP 01</div>
      <h3>Organize Your Time</h3>
      <p>
        Create a realistic schedule and divide large assignments
        into smaller tasks. Start with one thing at a time.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-number">TIP 02</div>
      <h3>Take Breaks</h3>
      <p>
        Give yourself time to rest between activities.
        Short breaks can help you return to your work with
        a clearer mind.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-number">TIP 03</div>
      <h3>Set Realistic Goals</h3>
      <p>
        You do not need to do everything perfectly.
        Focus on achievable goals and recognize your progress.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-number">TIP 04</div>
      <h3>Talk to Someone</h3>
      <p>
        Sharing your concerns with a trusted person can help
        you feel less alone when things become difficult.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- SELF ESTEEM -->

<section id="selfesteem">
  <div class="section-label">03 — PERSONAL GROWTH</div>
  <h2>Building Self-Esteem</h2>

  <p class="description">
    Self-esteem is connected to how we see and value ourselves.
    Developing a positive relationship with yourself takes time,
    patience and practice.
  </p>

  <div class="cards">

    <div class="card yellow">
      <div class="card-number">01</div>
      <h3>Stop Comparing Yourself</h3>
      <p>
        Everyone has a different journey. Focus on your own
        experiences instead of comparing your life with others.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card blue">
      <div class="card-number">02</div>
      <h3>Recognize Your Strengths</h3>
      <p>
        Remember your achievements, interests and abilities.
        Small accomplishments deserve recognition, too.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card purple">
      <div class="card-number">03</div>
      <h3>Learn From Mistakes</h3>
      <p>
        Making mistakes is part of learning. They do not
        determine your worth or define who you are.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- HEALTHY HABITS -->

<section id="habits" class="highlight">
  <div class="section-label">04 — DAILY WELL-BEING</div>
  <h2>Healthy Habits</h2>

  <p class="description">
    Taking care of your mental health also means creating
    everyday habits that support your general well-being.
  </p>

  <div class="cards">

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-number">REST</div>
      <h3>Prioritize Sleep</h3>
      <p>
        Try to maintain a regular sleep routine and give
        yourself enough time to relax before bedtime.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-number">INTERESTS</div>
      <h3>Enjoy Your Hobbies</h3>
      <p>
        Make time for activities you enjoy, such as reading,
        drawing, listening to music or spending time outdoors.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-number">CONNECTION</div>
      <h3>Stay Connected</h3>
      <p>
        Build supportive relationships with friends,
        family members and people who respect you.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- SUPPORT -->

<section id="support">
  <div class="section-label">05 — YOU ARE NOT ALONE</div>
  <h2>Asking for Help Is Okay</h2>

  <p class="description">
    Sometimes, taking care of yourself means recognizing
    when you need support from someone else.
  </p>

  <div class="support-box">
    <h3>Who Can You Talk To?</h3>

    <p>
      If your emotions or problems become difficult to manage,
      consider talking to a trusted adult, family member,
      teacher, school counselor or qualified mental health
      professional. You deserve to be listened to and supported.
    </p>

    <br>

    <p>
      Remember: asking for help is not a weakness.
      It is a positive step towards taking care of yourself.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FINAL MESSAGE -->

<section class="highlight">
  <div class="quote">
    <p>
      "You do not have to be okay every single day.
      Give yourself the same care and understanding
      you would give to someone else."
    </p>
    <span>MIND MATTERS — YOUR WELL-BEING COUNTS</span>
  </div>
</section>

<footer>
  <h2>MIND MATTERS.</h2>
  <div class="footer-line"></div>
  <p>A student project promoting mental health awareness.</p>
  <p>Be kind to yourself. Be kind to others.</p>
  <p style="margin-top:20px;font-size:11px;">
    This website is an educational resource and does not replace
    professional mental health support.
  </p>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
